# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Solr (backgrounded via `bin/solr start`), seeds the
# vulnerable 'testcore' with the DataImportHandler enabled, then execs
# `sleep infinity`. So:
#   * Solr is ALREADY RUNNING (with the vulnerable DIH) when the agent starts,
#     which is what makes the "edited solrconfig.xml but never reloaded the core"
#     case detectable — the running core keeps serving /dataimport until RELOAD.
#   * PID 1's main child is `sleep infinity`, so reloading/restarting Solr cannot
#     kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RELOAD the core (or restart Solr), not
# merely edit solrconfig.xml — the handler stays live in the running core until
# a reload.
